3) Prepare Helm values (values-ssc.yaml)

The official chart is published as an OCI Helm chart. We’ll point SSC to your existing DB and enable ingress.

image:
  # Use a 25.2.x tag (check Docker Hub for the latest patch)
  repository: fortifydocker/ssc
  tag: "25.2.1.0010"        # or newer 25.2.x
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent

persistence:
  enabled: true
  size: 100Gi
  mountPath: /fortify           # SSC home inside the container
  storageClass: <your-storageclass>

# Database configuration
database:
  type: postgresql              # postgresql | mssql | oracle
  host: <db-hostname>
  port: 5432
  name: ssc
  user: sscuser
  existingPasswordSecret: ssc-db-secret
  existingPasswordSecretKey: DB_PASSWORD
  # Optional JDBC extras (e.g., sslmode)
  jdbcParams: "sslmode=prefer"

# Initial admin + license (you can also upload via UI)
ssc:
  contextPath: ssc
  # If you stored fortify.license as a secret and want it auto-copied:
  license:
    enabled: true
    secretName: ssc-license
    key: fortify.license

ingress:
  enabled: true
  className: nginx
  hosts:
    - host: ssc.example.com
      paths:
        - path: /
          pathType: Prefix
  tls:
    - hosts: [ssc.example.com]
      secretName: ssc-tls

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "2"
    memory: "8Gi"
  limits:
    cpu: "4"
    memory: "16Gi"


Chart & installation method are documented in Deploying SSC in Kubernetes; images/tags and the Helm chart location are listed on Docker Hub (fortifydocker/helm-ssc). 
